language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ A merchant's weight broke into n pieces of whole-pound weights; the pieces together weigh m pounds and can weigh every whole weight from 1 to m on a balance.
given m : int(1..100)
given n : int(1..10)
find weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..m)
find c : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..n)] of int(-1..1)

branching on [weights]

such that
$ the pieces are listed in increasing order and no two pieces have the same weight
allDiff(weights),
forAll i : int(1..n-1) . weights[i] < weights[i+1],
$ the pieces together weigh the whole weight
(sum i : int(1..n) . weights[i]) = m,
$ every whole weight k from 1 to m can be weighed: each piece is on the object's pan (-1), on the other pan (+1) or not used (0), so the signed sum of pieces is k
forAll k : int(1..m) . (sum i : int(1..n) . c[k,i] * weights[i]) = k
